      "summary": [
        {
          "text": "72-year-old Caucasian man had an ulcerated polypoid right-calf lesion excised. Histology showed a dermal nodular epithelioid neoplasm with retiform empty pseudovascular spaces, severe atypia, high mitotic activity and 12 mm Breslow thickness. S100/Melan-A were diffusely positive while cytokeratin and vascular markers were negative. NRAS Q61R c.182A>G at 30% VAF supported melanoma diagnosis; other mutations above 5% VAF were not detected.",
